.TH CVECTOR_APPEND_CVECTOR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_append_cvector \- append vector to vector
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cvector.h>

bool cvector_append_cvector(cvec v_to, cvec v_from);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Appends all elements from one vector to another. Both vectors must have
the same element size.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v_to    Destination vector
v_from  Source vector
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns true on success
Returns false if memory allocation fails
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Element sizes must match (asserts if different)
All elements are appended or none
Automatically reserves capacity if needed
Asserts if v_to or v_from is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_append_cvec (3),
.BR cvector_append_array (3)
